We chose keychains because they were practical to produce within the project window. Our primary audience was **NEU students**, with students from other universities as a secondary group. Proximity made it easier to reach buyers and build relevant products and communication.

I **designed and distributed a quick customer survey** to explore demand and willingness to pay. The finding of approximately **VND 50,000** informed the team's **VND 49,000 selling price**. It was a practical pricing input for this project, rather than a representative estimate of the student market.

I helped combine the team's early ideas into a customizable pixel character. Customers could choose details such as hair and clothing on the website. I worked with a graphic designer on the character assets and learned Aseprite for the pixel artwork. We launched with the website and a Google Form for orders.
